## Recommended repair, after agreement

1. **Record the authority.** Add manual 013 and its project-prompt pointer,
   explicitly extending 0160 to the shared elevation driver and focused scope
   regression coverage. Preserve manual 012's product repair and normal-resume
   exception. Update the repository's elevation usage guidance to describe the
   new default. Record this as a consumer gate coverage defect, including the
   mixed committed/uncommitted reproducer, rather than claiming an ASG patch.

2. **Fix the invoked driver.** With neither `-Project`, `-All` nor an explicit
   `-Base`, select every in-scope product project through the existing analysis
   pipeline. Preserve explicit-base union with working-tree changes, dependent
   expansion, explicit selection, exclusions and failure handling. Handle
   `-ScopeOnly` before any success verdict. Add a focused PowerShell regression
   harness under `Elevation/`, outside MTP discovery, using fixture data and
   controlled Git responses; keep its output under this arc's `.artifacts/`.
   Cover clean, report-only, test-only and mixed trees, explicit base and invalid
   base, global triggers, `-All`, `-Project`, dependent closure and inspection
   output. Do not introduce constructor test identities or change Git history.

3. **Measure the real path.** Run all fifteen unchanged 0160 gates in their
   existing evaluator/census context. Require actual analysis and readable
   reports from all twelve current product projects, zero new findings under
   the existing ELEV004 exclusion, exactly 1,136 passing constructor cases,
   the exact census, zero failures/skips and no owned-code warnings. Check the
   full analysis against the existing gate time budget. Preserve every retained
   product regression and the seven-deletion/one-migration/one-addition effects.

4. **Complete the handoff and wait for the operator's commit.** Validate all
   494 steps; refresh the profile-1 receipt for the prompt pointer while proving
   all 988 compiled artifacts unchanged. Record implementation, scope regression
   results and gate measurements in the manual and slice handoff. Prepare the
   operator reply under `.artifacts/0160-02-operator-repair/`. Preserve published
   requirements, frozen descriptors, analyzer rules/known-findings, supervisor
   counters, expected-red records, checkpoints/case evidence, contract registries,
   versions/lock and ASG/STL source. Do not launch during the repair.

The cost is broader analysis on subsequent slices. That is a deliberate tradeoff:
the existing frozen command supplies no reliable base. A fallback only when zero
targets are selected would leave mixed trees unsound. Injecting guessed branch
or manifest history into this general driver would add a separate coupling.
Changing the frozen descriptors to use `-Base {step_base}` could preserve narrower
selection but requires a different contract-amendment decision. I recommend the
driver fix above for this arc, with explicit-base selection still available.

